      {
        "id": 126904,
        "name": "Killswitch",
        "username": "Killswitch",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/{size}/2116_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-12T14:41:52.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The number of targets you can destroy is infinite.</p>\n<p>SPOLERS BELOW</p>\n<p>[color=white]Runes of Malediction + Relic Spirit combo.</p>\n<p>[color=white]Fixer: Jack Handle, Alternating Tiger Claw, Harmony, Bloody Knuckles</p>\n<p>[color=white]Legacy: Inspiring Prescence + Galvanize</p>\n<p>[color=white]Visionary: Twist the Ether x2- Mr. Fixer</p>\n<p>[color=white]Insula Primalis-Obsidian Field</p>\n<p><font color=\"white\">Fixer deals 9 irreducable damage to the runes, which revive the relic spirit, which revive the runes again. Assuming this isn't just a silly loophole to the puzzle, this should count as destroying as many targets as possible in a turn. This kind of damage should K.O. nearly every target with at least 9 HP without worrying about damage reduction, so I don't know how many targets that would be.</font>[/color][/color][/color][/color][/color]</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:01:26.112Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
